# Round 91: `zeros of N` was compiled as `buffer of N` on the belief they
# make "the same length-N zero buffer". They do not: this VM's `zeros` is a
# TENSOR builtin returning a LIST, and `buffer` returns a VAL_BUFFER --
# different type, printing, shape, and builtin dispatch. Sixteen fixtures
# used `zeros` and every one touched the container ONLY through indexed
# read/write, `len of`, and reductions, where a 1-D zero list and a 1-D
# zero buffer are indistinguishable: invariant 7's nastier form, a
# fixtured path with no DISCRIMINATING fixture. This one discriminates on
# every axis at once. (The old comment blamed an arena clobber for the
# substitution; measured this round, emitting the real callee is clean.)
z is zeros of 3
b is buffer of 3
print of (type of z)
print of (type of b)
print of z
print of b
z[0] is 1
z[1] is 2
print of z
print of (len of z)
print of (sum of z)
print of (norm of z)
w is zeros of 3
w[0] is 3
w[1] is 4
print of (dot of [z, w])
m is zeros of [2, 3]
print of m
print of (type of m)
print of (len of m)
print of (sum of z[0 : 2])
print of (norm of z[0 : 2])
